{
  "id": "m24l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "itertools: combinar iterables",
    "en": "itertools: combining iterables"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Herramientas para iterar"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`itertools` ofrece utilidades eficientes para recorrer datos. `chain` une varios iterables en uno solo."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from itertools import chain",
          "print(list(chain([1, 2], [3, 4])))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[1, 2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`chain.from_iterable(listas)` aplana una lista de listas. `combinations(items, n)` da todas las combinaciones de tamaño n (sin repetir orden)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from itertools import combinations",
          "print(list(combinations(['a', 'b', 'c'], 2)))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[('a', 'b'), ('a', 'c'), ('b', 'c')]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Estas funciones devuelven iteradores perezosos; envuélvelas en list() para verlas."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Tools for iterating"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`itertools` provides efficient utilities to traverse data. `chain` joins several iterables into one."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from itertools import chain",
          "print(list(chain([1, 2], [3, 4])))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[1, 2, 3, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`chain.from_iterable(lists)` flattens a list of lists. `combinations(items, n)` gives all size-n combinations (order doesn't repeat)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from itertools import combinations",
          "print(list(combinations(['a', 'b', 'c'], 2)))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[('a', 'b'), ('a', 'c'), ('b', 'c')]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "These return lazy iterators; wrap them in list() to see them."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m24l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `aplanar(listas)` que reciba una lista de listas y devuelva una sola lista con todos los elementos (usa itertools.chain).",
        "en": "Define `aplanar(listas)` taking a list of lists and returning a single list with all elements (use itertools.chain)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from itertools import chain",
        "",
        "def aplanar(listas):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from itertools import chain",
        "",
        "def aplanar(listas):",
        "    return list(chain.from_iterable(listas))"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "chain.from_iterable recorre cada sublista en orden."
        ],
        "en": [
          "chain.from_iterable goes through each sublist in order."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "aplanar",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [
                    1,
                    2
                  ],
                  [
                    3
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                1,
                2,
                3
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [],
                  [
                    5
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                5
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                []
              ],
              "expected": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m24l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `parejas(items)` que devuelva todas las combinaciones de 2 elementos, cada una como lista (usa itertools.combinations).",
        "en": "Define `parejas(items)` returning all 2-element combinations, each as a list (use itertools.combinations)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from itertools import combinations",
        "",
        "def parejas(items):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from itertools import combinations",
        "",
        "def parejas(items):",
        "    return [list(c) for c in combinations(items, 2)]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "combinations da tuplas; conviértelas a list."
        ],
        "en": [
          "combinations yields tuples; convert them to list."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "parejas",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  "a",
                  "b",
                  "c"
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                [
                  "a",
                  "b"
                ],
                [
                  "a",
                  "c"
                ],
                [
                  "b",
                  "c"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  "x"
                ]
              ],
              "expected": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}